      "transcript_text": "Now let us look at as to how the cash flows between the financial markets on the one hand and the corporation on the other hand. What is a firm? A firm as you understand is a bundle of real assets. And what is the financial market? Financial market comprises of investors like UNM, who are holding financial assets such as shares and bonds. So we have firm on the one hand and we have financial markets on the other hand and we have financial manager in between. First of all cash is raised by the financial manager from the financial market. market. Then this cash is used to purchase real assets. This cash is invested into the firm. Now once these real assets produce goods and services and once these goods and services are sold to the customers of the company cash is generated. Here the financial manager has to make a choice. Either a part of this cash that has been generated can be retained and reinvested back into the firm. Alternatively another part can be paid out as dividend to shareholders or it can be returned in another form to investors.",
