      "notes_markdown": "# CF M02 C22 Connecting the Four Present Value Shortcuts\n\n> **Core Takeaway:** The growing annuity formula is the master key; setting G=0 or T=∞ collapses it into the standard perpetuity and annuity present value formulas.\n### Valuation Rules & Criteria\n- **Growing Annuity PV:** `PV = C / (R - G) × [1 - (1 + G)/(1 + R)^T]` (requires G ≠ R)\n- **Ordinary NVD PV:** Setting G=0 yields `PV = C/R × [1 - 1/(1+R)^T]`, matching the standard NVD formula.\n- **Growing Perpetuity PV:** With T=∞ and G<R, the term `(1+G)/(1+R)^∞ → 0`, simplifying to `PV = C / (R - G)`.\n- **Ordinary Perpetuity PV:** With T=∞ and G=0, the formula collapses to `PV = C / R`, matching the standard perpetuity formula.\n\n### MCQ Trap Radar\n1. **Trap:** The growing perpetuity formula `C/(R-G)` applies to any cash flow stream with growth. **Reality:** It only applies when T=∞ **and** G<R; otherwise, the finite-T formula must be used.\n2. **Trap:** Setting G=0 in the growing annuity formula always gives the ordinary perpetuity value. **Reality:** It gives the ordinary perpetuity value **only if T=∞**; finite T with G=0 yields an ordinary annuity, not a perpetuity.",
      "mcqs_json": "[]",
      "subjectives_json": "[]",
      "flashcards_json": "[]",
      "slides_json": "[]",
