      "notes_markdown": "# CF M03 C14 Yield to Maturity and Realised Bond Returns\n\n> **Core Takeaway:** If YTM remains unchanged, the realized holding-period return equals the initial YTM; if YTM rises, the realized return falls below the initial YTM.\n### Yield to Maturity and Realised Bond Returns Principles\n- **Price today ($P_0$) at 3% YTM:** $110.834 (calculated as $\\frac{5}{0.03}\\left[1 - \\frac{1}{1.03^6}\\right] + \\frac{1000}{1.03^6}$).\n- **Price 1 year from today ($P_1$) at 3% YTM:** $109.159 (calculated as $\\frac{5}{0.03}\\left[1 - \\frac{1}{1.03^6}\\right] + \\frac{1000}{1.03^6}$ with 5 remaining periods).\n- **Realized return formula:** $\\frac{C + P_1 - P_0}{P_0}$.\n- **Result:** With $C = \\$5$, $P_0 = \\$110.834$, $P_1 = \\$109.159$, the realized return is exactly **3%**, matching the initial YTM.\n\n### YTM and Return Relationship\n- **YTM unchanged → Realized return = YTM.** (As demonstrated: 3% YTM → 3% realized return.)\n- **YTM increases → Realized return < initial YTM.** (Rising yields cause price depreciation that erodes the holding-period return.)\n\n### MCQ Trap Radar\n1. **Trap:** A higher coupon rate guarantees a higher realized return regardless of yield changes. → **Reality:** Realized return depends on the change in YTM relative to the initial YTM, not just the coupon.\n2. **Trap:** If a bond is held to maturity, the realized return will always equal the YTM at purchase. → **Reality:** The realized return equals the YTM only if the YTM remains constant over the holding period; changing yields alter the actual return.",
      "mcqs_json": "[{\"id\": 1, \"question\": \"An investor purchases a bond at a price of $P_0$ when the YTM is 4% per annum. One year later, market YTM rises to 5%. Assuming the bond has a positive coupon, what happens to the investor's realized return over that one-year holding period compared to the initial YTM of 4%?\", \"options\": [\"A) The realized return will be exactly 4% because the coupon is fixed.\", \"B) The realized return will be slightly above 4% due to the coupon payment.\", \"C) The realized return will be below 4% because the bond's price has fallen due to the rise in YTM.\", \"D) The realized return cannot be determined without knowing the bond's maturity.\"], \"explanation\": \"\", \"key_concept\": \"\"}]",
