          "difficulty": "Moderate | Conceptual",
          "explanation": "The correct answer is B) Cash Outflow (Negative sign). The lecture explicitly states: \"If your networking capital goes up, it is essentially going to be a cash outflow. And therefore, it will have a negative sign.\" This is because tying up more cash in operations reduces the cash available to the firm today. Option A is the Trap 1 sign confusion distractor. Option C is incorrect as a change always has an effect. Option D is a distractor for students who overthink a straightforward rule.",
          "key_concept": "Cash Flow Sign Rule"
