          "correct_index": 1,
          "difficulty": "Easy | Core Intuition",
          "explanation": "The correct answer is B) When the firm pays suppliers for raw materials. The lecture explicitly asks: \"can you let me know when does the cash go out of business?\" and answers: \"Obviously if you look here, this is the point in time. When the cash goes out of business.\" The lecture describes this as the point where the firm makes payment to suppliers for the purchase of raw materials. Option A is a distractor as selling goods on credit typically delays cash outflow, not triggers the initial outflow. Option C refers to the end, not the start of the cycle.",
          "key_concept": "Cash Outflow Timing"
