          "correct_index": 1,
          "difficulty": "Moderate | Tricky",
          "explanation": "The correct answer is B) Security B offers higher expected return per unit of risk. This tests the concept that for the same expected return, lower standard deviation (volatility) implies better risk-adjusted performance. The coefficient of variation (CV = SD/Expected Return) for A is 20/12 = 1.67, and for B is 5/12 = 0.42, confirming B has lower relative risk. Distractor A is incorrect because risk-averse investors prefer lower volatility for the same return. Distractor C is incorrect as 20% > 5%. Distractor D is incorrect as CV is higher for A.",
