          "correct_index": 1,
          "difficulty": "Easy | Conceptual",
          "explanation": "The correct answer is B) The analyst ignored the probabilities of each state occurring. This directly tests Trap 2 from the MCQ Trap Radar. The lecture explicitly defines expected return as the summation of P_i × R_i. A simple average assumes all states are equally likely (25% each), which contradicts the given probabilities of 25%, 50%, and 25%. Distractor A is a procedural error not relevant to the conceptual framework. Distractor C introduces an unnecessary statistical modification. Distractor D is the incorrect distractor.",
