          "explanation": "From the formula σ²p = x₁²σ₁² + x₂²σ₂² + 2x₁x₂ρ₁₂σ₁σ₂, the covariance term is 2x₁x₂ρ₁₂σ₁σ₂. Since ρ₁₂ is multiplied by this term, if ρ₁₂ decreases (becomes more negative), the value of the covariance term decreases (becomes more negative). Since this term is added to the variance components, a more negative value reduces the total portfolio variance. This reflects the benefit of diversification when stocks move in opposite directions.",
