          "explanation": "When ρ₁₂ = -1, the formula for portfolio standard deviation is σp = |x₁σ₁ - x₂σ₂|. σp becomes zero only when the weighted standard deviations are exactly equal (x₁σ₁ = x₂σ₂). If x₁ increases and x₂ decreases, the difference |x₁σ₁ - x₂σ₂| will change depending on the relative magnitudes of σ₁ and σ₂. It will not always increase or decrease. The student must recognize the boundary condition for risk elimination under perfect negative correlation.",
