          "correct_index": 2,
          "explanation": "When ρ₁₂ = +1, the portfolio variance formula simplifies to (x₁σ₁ + x₂σ₂)². This means the portfolio standard deviation is the weighted average of the individual standard deviations. Since variance is the square of standard deviation, the portfolio variance is effectively the weighted sum of variances plus the cross-term, which results in no risk reduction beyond the linear weighting. ρ₁₂ = 0 implies uncorrelated returns, which actually provides some diversification benefit (variance is lower than the weighted sum). ρ₁₂ = -1 implies the potential for maximum risk reduction.",
          "key_concept": "ρ = +1 eliminates diversification; ρ = 0 or -1 provides benefits."
