          "difficulty": "Moderate | Sensitivity",
          "explanation": "The formula for beta derived in the lecture is Beta = ρ_I,M × σ_I / σ_M. Here, beta is directly proportional to the correlation coefficient ρ_I,M. If ρ decreases (becomes less positive or more negative), the product ρ × σ_I decreases, leading to a lower beta value. Option A is the distractor for incorrectly assuming an inverse relationship. Option C is the distractor for ignoring the correlation term. Option D is the distractor for confusing a decrease in correlation with a sign change, which would only happen if ρ crossed zero into negative territory significantly.",
