          "explanation": "The lecture's central thesis was the distinction between ownership and management. The professor stated: \"Management, on the other hand, is about how the company is being run. Now, it can be run by other family members who may or may not be owners, or it can be run by completely outside professionals.\" The four-quadrant classification model was built on the premise that these two dimensions vary independently. Option A is incorrect because the lecture gave the example of TCS, where high family ownership exists alongside professional management. Option C is incorrect because professional management does not necessarily dilute ownership; TCS has 70% family ownership with professional management. Option D is incorrect because the Apollo Hospitals example showed control can exist without majority percentage.",
