      "transcript_text": "In the systems theory, an organisation is viewed as a unified, interconnected and a purpose-driven mechanism of parts. That is repeat, these are three things that are important here. An organisation is viewed as interconnected as very significant. very purpose-driven and seen as unified as a mechanism which has these three elements and rather than something which is isolated or a very rigid entity. It is supposed to be something which is interconnected. There are actually four parts to an organisation. The components I would say as an organisation that when we break up this theory comes out. One is there are inputs. There is a transformation process. There is an output and there is a feedback. So, system-sary considers all of this saying as part of inputs, the system will consist of what are the parts involved, the supplier, the raw materials. So, these are the kind of parts that will involve as part of the input mechanism. Then there is a transformation mechanism. Transformation mechanism is what, how does the input get converted to an output? It could use machine-based machinery, it could use people, it could use some kind of technology. So, all this is the way how raw material is converted to a finished good. It goes through an entire process. All that is part of the transformation. The output component is what is the final output that is an organisational finally, give to a customer or sell to a customer. Finished good or a finished service can be both good services. So, that is what is the output component. output component. The fourth component as the feedback component which is the reverse loop where the customer shares feedback or the person receiving the finished goods or finished service receives shares feedback which looks back and has a change in all the four components. You could decide to change the raw material basis that you could change decide to change the process basis the feedback. So, these are the four core components. All this put together are the components of a company again all these are interconnected and all these lead to a purpose purpose which is delivering a certain finished good or a service to the customer and they work in unison. So, this is the systems theory definition of a company. Then there are two kinds of systems that you could talk about something you could have you would have heard there are open systems and there are closed systems. One systems are ones which also interact with their external environment while closed systems interact within themselves. A closed system will only be interacting within the employees within lecture manufacturing within their own within their own teams etcetera. They have no purview they have no visibility to the external environment at all. What happens in such a system they do not know what is happening outside world they have little linkage to the market they may not be in keeping in pace with what the market wants or the customer wants. Quite possible that they will stagnate or eventually decline. An open system is something that has an external view also continuously interacts with external world knows what is happening in the external world and makes changes accordingly to its own system interacts with customers and then basis feedback makes changes an external orientation gives it a more dynamic things. Now, why are we talking open system and closed system? We want to understand what is the family businesses is the family business and open system or a closed system actually it is a mix of both because we are not talking one entity we are talking family and business again that is two different components out here. The business is an open system for sure. The business has to interact with its customers business has to interact with its suppliers it is dependent on what happens in the external environment it is subject to market risks all these are characteristics of an open system. The family meanwhile can be a closed system sometimes it is much more concerned with what is happening within what are the dynamics within the family it runs a lot more than emotions. Desitions taken are not keeping in what the business wants or the external world wants but within keeping sometimes the family legacy family control lot of this player roll out there actually there are three components here while we talk about in in systems series we talked about four components when it comes to family there are three other components or three other inter dependent groups which play a role or inter dependent system which can play a role ownership management and family. So far we have discussed family has its own system most likely a closed system we have talked about business or management which is likely an open system because it interacts with customers there is a third component here called ownership. Now the owners have their own view of the business and what the business where the business likely is to go and what do they want from the business what they define as the value that they seek for the business shareholder value we talk of the shareholder here is a family owner what their values are and what they see as going forward in the business. These are the three interconnected parts when we have to see system series for the family and how the interconnection between these three components go a long way in defining how the family goes forward and that is the essence of the system series for the family business.",
