          "difficulty": "Moderate | Application",
          "explanation": "The lecture specifically mentions Infosys: \"Over 2 million shareholders holding over 4 billion shares (illustrates why owners cannot run daily operations and must delegate authority to professional managers).\" This example underscores the delegation dilemma in large ownership structures, a key theme in family business strategy regarding the separation of ownership and management.",
          "key_concept": "Ownership vs. Management Delegation"
