          "correct_index": 1,
          "difficulty": "Easy | Conceptual",
          "explanation": "The lecturer explicitly stated: \"Succession we have spoken about is not an event. It is a journey. It is something that takes place over time in which case the incumbent has to plan in terms of how he or she can let go.\" The glide path concept involves the incumbent consciously transitioning from active operator to mentor/adviser role, and picking up activities outside the business so they are not \"glued to the business.\" Option A focuses on legal process, which was not the lecturer's point. Option C imposes a specific timeline not mentioned. Option D references government regulation not discussed.",
