      "transcript_text": "What are the key dimensions that we can look at to understand if the succession has been successful? You can look at it from three ways from the three circle diagram itself will give you a good idea. You can see the implications on the family. You can see the implications on management and the you can see the implications on external stakeholders and also see the implications on the firm. All these are you can see how they impact. The family first you can see the family being a lot more united. The bonding has actually grown. The amount of engagement between the family has continued to increase. There are no conflicts arising. So these are ways you can see that actually the succession has actually worked. Harmony is something that the family business is. Family puts a premium on. That is something that has worked well as part of the succession. It is something that you can clearly see. For the others, take hold. As well as changes in how the family's engagement with social and broader communities, what are the changes over there? How is the firm's performance? How is it grow? How is it return on its capital? What is the profit margin? All that will tell you how the firm is doing well. That is an easier one to measure. There is also an entrepreneurial side. When you look at it from an entrepreneurial family galaxy and putting the family at the center, the new initiatives that get created. How are the person who is being engaged with them? Are you able to raise external funding? Are you able to engage other external stakeholders in driving new entrepreneurial opportunities? All of these are very good indicators if the succession has been successful or not.",
