      "transcript_text": "So, we make as a framework of best practices for succession process. What all would it entail? It would entail four parts. The first part is to plan for the succession itself. The second part is identifying the potential successors and providing them with import, or that they are groomed. One of them is then chosen as the successor. And finally, you have to close the entire process and hand over. It is probably the last step as the... And in this entire process, while all of this is happening, there are another two very important dimensions, which span the entire process itself of management of relationships, both within the family as well as with external stakeholders.",
