      "transcript_text": "One interesting case we should discuss is what happens when we have a working couple inside the family form, and in both husband and wife are working in the same family form. Both are ambitious, they are only one family firm, in which case, what happens. Who decides? Who is this? will inside the family firm as in both husband and wife are working in the same family firm both are ambitious both have carriers this only one family firm in which case what happens who decides whose thoughts come first whose carrier come first. So these are things that can take an interesting term sometimes what we look at is three kinds of models where we have couples working in a family firm and let us look like how each of them looks inside a family firm. We look at who is actually firm it is and it can be either her firm or his firm and how does the spur how does the spouse work in it or does not work in it and what car the how does it look like in such cases. We also look like how what kind of conversations each working couple need to have in such cases. So, the three models are let us say primary secondary model this kind of a model in which there is a primary carrier there is a secondary carrier that is what it means in which case there is always one carrier which means any conflict inside a family firm what how it pans out it is actually basically his firm and she runs the back office or equivalent of that. This being secondary a choice at all or the way it is entirely designed that you are always designed to come second or there is always somebody who will win any battle one that is one model second model is turn taking the priority alternates on a certain schedule some phase is something she will lead some phase he will lead this is like somewhat like the rotating chief ministers we have in Indian politics except that that does not happen. The first chief minister who comes serve student of yours does not resign for the next one to come. So, is the turn ever being honored is a question that will happen or one person decides to continue forever. The third is the double primary neither one yields each is very ambitious and both want to take their carrier up to the next level both have significant growth path charted out for each of them and both matter to the firm as well. So, there is bound to be some amount of conflict we need an arbitrator in that case who will arbitrate who will ensure that these clashes do not get out of control usually you will see that every family which has a working couple will have one of these we have to find a way out of this that is the design question that we are talking about have to find a way out. The second part we said we will address is whose firm is it and does the spouse work in it. So, here we have two cases it is his family firm or her family firm and then we have a case whether there the spouse is working in the firm or spouse is working outside the firm. Let us take a case where it is his family firm and the spouse is elsewhere as in the spouse is not in the family firm in the husband's family firm or the wife's family firm in this case it is his family firm this the husband's family firm in which case the firm is his and the spouse is free to work whichever way they want wherever they want and the husband's decisions are also not question because only one person is in the family firm. This is an area what I would call a free agent case where both are free to do what they want. Now let us take a look where it is her family firm and the spouse is inside the firm and the firm is not Japanese in which case no the son-in-law is actually the CEO of his a Japanese one but let us take an Indian firm example in this case it is her family firm. So the son-in-law he is a son-in-law in the firm son-in-law has joined the in-law's business but she is the owner she has the air and he will join because he brings certain skills to the table and it is much valued and that is why he is in the family firm in some way it also ensures that there is family harmony but can you question the son-in-law to deeply is something to debate the in-laws generally do not question the son-in-law to my dad is Indian culture right. So it is some amount of neportism can creep in and that is something to be watched out for. Similarly if it is his family firm and the spouse is there in the firm it is more like somebody who can keep the trust it is a she is a co-personer as a result of Indian laws but in case it is her family firm and spouse is elsewhere her spouse the guy is working outside the business then it is very clear for her she is the successor she is the one who will inherit the firm and there is no not necessary that we need to have done taking in this case this could be a case which is a double primary where husband is pursuing a carrier outside ambitious she is also ambitious but she is doing inside the family firm. We have to understand as to which family firm that you are getting into fits which kind of of these cells and therefore what is your role there each of these roles will have implications on what you will bring to that work there how is how what are the kind of responsibilities you will have to undertake as part of this and something that you can map out as a result of these forms. Let us step to the conversations every couple working in a family business needs to have the first is priority what are we talking here who is carrier comes first or for how long or can they keep changing back and forth can like you said turn taking can happen out here where at some stage somebody moves for first and then comes back and the other person gets priority for carrier money who is who is running who is paid who earns what more importantly who is unpaid for the role that is who is going to be unpaid for even spite of doing a role out there needs to be clear boundaries what needs to be discussed at home what needs to be discussed at office we have spoken earlier about boardroom coming to dining room and vice versa what need this be clarity on what cannot be discussed at home invariably there will be some things percolating between the two but has to be kept at a minimum title it is important to understand what role each place what is the kind of pay and what is the kind of credit each gets to be in the firm if they are working in the same family firm it should not be an issue where the role is completely out of sync with the pay or the credit does not ensure to the person doing the hard job out there. So let us understand while the two people are owners do not have to be in similar kind of roles or at the same level each one can be a different skill set different qualification also but whatever role they do should be commensurate with the pay and the credit they get for that lastly these are not constant right so as the family state changes there are children there are school going kids there are elders at home to be taken care of some of these roles will change. So as a result of it there needs to be some kind of back and forth sometimes renegotiation or at what stage can this be transferred what kind of who to be transferred to what is the succession roadmap all these needs to be a review that needs to be done throughout the journey of this working couple in the family business. So in summary we have discussed three models and five conversations that every working couple in a family business needs to happen.",
