          "explanation": "The lecture highlights the practical lesson from the V.B. Rangaraj versus V.B. Gopalkrishnan case: a transfer restriction only in the shareholders' agreement and not also in the articles of association may be unenforceable against the company. The articles of association need to reflect and agree with what is in the shareholders' agreement, as the articles are more important.",
          "key_concept": "Enforceability Trap - India Case Law"
