          "difficulty": "Moderate | Sensitivity",
          "explanation": "The lecture explains that a super majority, often 75%, is required for very consequential decisions including amendments to the shareholders' agreement. Shifting the threshold from simple majority toward unanimity increases decision-making friction, making it harder for the majority to impose decisions on the minority.",
