      "transcript_text": "So, in summary, we have seen how governance differs across the three circles. We have seen governance in the family circle, we have seen governance in the business circle, and we have seen governance in the management circle. Governance has three distinct jobs, and each one, each structure, each circle has its own structure. Each has their own characteristics, which is why the structures in each, each of the circles are different. And if we leave every of those circles to informal methods, then each circle will fail in its own different way. So if you were to compare the three circles the business circle, what the kind of institutions it requires are the board. What it does is it, it rolls out the purpose the composition of committees, all that the board will, will include. Will ensure it, it monitors the basic purpose the family was for. The family circle has probably the richest set of vehicles that are there. We talked about the forum, the council, the constitution. There's a whole host of it. So family circle is probably the maximum number of vehicles that are result, that are required for the governance. Ownership is about a lot more about ownership types, the kind of agreements that are required, the and how do you take care of the shareholder assembly, the galaxy. So these are some amount of the vehicles that are required at the ownership circles. Each circle, as we see, has a very different set of institutions that are required. Each one have their ownings their own governance mechanisms, and each one have their own outcomes that are desired as a result of that circle. What combines is that all these governance mechanisms across three circles, it's better that we call it out at what stage they are required. It's better to document each of it. It's better to ensure that the entire family agrees on each, each one of those. Informality works only to a certain extent. It is also important that each of these institutions are revisited at a frequent interval. So that each of these can function as the family changes As the generation passes down the line, we find that the changes are required in each of these, even though they are written down. So there must be a mechanism built inside where it sees that each of these can therefore be modified, aligned to the requirement of that date, of that generation, of that market. Ensure that the fundamental objective of the family business is to ensure succession, ensure longevity of the family firm, and the business is ensured.",
