          "difficulty": "Easy | Conceptual",
          "explanation": "The lecture explicitly states that evidence must be relevant to the question under discussion. The professor gave this exact example: employee satisfaction scores from Bangalore do not support the claim of opening a new office in Hyderabad, even if the numbers are accurate. The scores from one office do not logically bridge to a claim about a different location.",
