          "explanation": "The lecture used the one million downloads example to show that this evidence supports a claim about trial (many people were willing to try the app), but it does not prove that customers loved using it. The critical missing element is reasoning that connects the fact of downloads to the conclusion of enjoyment; without it, the audience might reasonably conclude the app is poor quality based on reviews.",
          "key_concept": "Evidence vs. Conclusion & Reasoning Gap"
