      "status": "completed",
      "notes_markdown": "# Confirmation Bias\n\n> **Core Takeaway:** Confirmation bias is the default cognitive tendency to favor information that supports existing beliefs while dismissing contradictions, and overcoming it requires structural processes, like actively seeking disconfirming evidence, rather than willpower.\n### Confirmation Bias Mechanisms\n- **Search & Notice:** Tendency to seek, notice, and interpret information that confirms pre-existing beliefs.\n- **Overlook & Dismiss:** Actively explain away or ignore contradictory evidence.\n- **System 1 → System 2 Loop:** System 1 forms an initial impression; System 2 defaults to finding reasons to justify that impression rather than critically testing it.\n- **Emotional Investment:** We spend more energy looking for reasons an idea will work than reasons it will fail, because confirming is cognitively easier than disconfirming.\n- **Business Contexts:** Manifests in leading market-research questions (e.g., \"Wouldn't you love a product that does X, Y, Z?\") and hiring, where snap judgments trigger unconscious evidence collection to justify the first impression.\n- **Mindset:** Our minds excel at building confident, coherent stories from limited evidence but struggle to ask, \"What evidence is missing?\"\n\n### Antidote\n- **Willpower is insufficient**, the bias operates before conscious awareness.\n- **Structural solution:** Build a habit of actively seeking disconfirming evidence.\n- **Pre-decision question:** \"What evidence would prove me wrong here? And have I actually gone looking for it?\"\n- **Formal process:** Assign a teammate to play devil's advocate on every major recommendation.\n\n### MCQ Trap Radar\n1. **Trap:** Confirmation bias only affects people with weak critical-thinking skills. → **Reality:** It operates automatically before conscious awareness, affecting even skilled professionals.\n2. **Trap:** The antidote to confirmation bias is simply \"trying harder\" to be objective. → **Reality:** Willpower fails because the bias operates pre-consciously; the fix requires structural processes like actively seeking disconfirming evidence.",
      "mcqs_json": "[{\"id\": 1, \"question\": \"Professor Kahneman connects confirmation bias directly to System 1 thinking. Which statement best describes the role of System 2 in this bias?\", \"options\": [\"A) System 2 critically evaluates and often disproves the System 1 impression.\", \"B) System 2 typically goes looking for reasons to justify the System 1 impression as correct.\", \"C) System 2 remains inactive until System 1 signals that a critical review is needed.\", \"D) System 2 overrides System 1 by applying deliberate logical analysis to the initial impression.\"], \"explanation\": \"\", \"key_concept\": \"\"}]",
      "subjectives_json": "[]",
