          "explanation": "The professor explained that credibility is established through data rigor: \"I have spoken to a statistically significant sample base... when you reach a number of 100 which essentially in statistics says gives you a 95% confidence level.\" This provides an objective anchor. Option A relies on authority, which the lecture cautioned against. Option C relies on subjective intuition, which the lecture argued against. Option D misrepresents the role of research as guaranteeing outcomes.",
          "key_concept": "Credibility through methodological rigor"
