          "explanation": "The lecture explicitly states: \"It can offer meaningful ownership but ownership is not the same as liquid wealth.\" This distinction is important for students to understand the nature of equity versus cash. Option A is incorrect because ownership does not guarantee immediate liquidity. Option B is incorrect because founding offers scope to shape direction, but the burden is on the founder; the lecture contrasts this with joining which offers less control. Option D is incorrect as ownership does not provide a salary.",
