          "explanation": "This directly challenges the common thought mentioned in the transcript: \"most successful founders are generally very young.\" The data shows the mean is 45, debunking the youth myth. Option B is incorrect because the research does not claim age has no correlation; it claims the correlation is with experience, not youth. Options C and D are factors associated with success but are not what the 45-year-old mean age statistic directly challenges.",
