          "explanation": "This tests the boundary condition and the concept of 'learning' discussed in the transcript. The text states: \"years of worked are not the same as years learned.\" Option A is the trap of assuming time equals learning. Option C is a trap reversing the transcript's logic. Option D is an extreme distractor; the transcript does not say corporate work is useless, but that the type of learning matters (e.g., Falguni Nayar learned business networks at Kotak).",
