          "difficulty": "Moderate | Tricky",
          "explanation": "The professor warns against being swayed by a founder's public persona. He advises looking for consistency between what the founder says (e.g., in podcasts or interviews) and the reality (e.g., early employee turnover, traction data from Crunchbase/MCA). If a founder talks about culture but loses early employees, they are sending a signal. The examiner tests the student's ability to see through the narrative to the underlying operational health.",
