      "notes_markdown": "# Synergy and Shareholder Wealth\n\n> **Core Takeaway:** Acquirers pay a premium above the target's fair value; the portion of total synergy retained by the acquirer equals synergy minus the premium, while the target retains the premium as its gain. On average, acquiring firm shareholders break even or lose value on a standalone basis, but combined firm shareholders typically see value creation.\n### Synergy And Shareholder Wealth\n- **Premium definition:** Price paid over and above the fair value of the target (`Premium = Offer Price − Fair Value`).\n- **Synergy sharing:** Acquirer retains `Synergy − Premium`; Target retains `Premium`.\n- **Loss condition:** If `Synergy < Premium`, the acquirer loses value.\n- **Target stock price reaction:** Jumps up upon announcement because shareholders will receive the offer price > pre-announcement price.\n- **Target price vs. offer price:** Target price usually settles below the offer price because of the probability the deal may not complete; higher completion probability pushes the price closer to the offer price.\n- **Acquirer shareholder outcome:** On average, acquiring firm shareholders do not benefit from M&A on a standalone basis, though combined firm shareholders typically see value creation.\n\n### Formulas & Worked Numerical\n- **Takeover premium (example):** If target = ₹100 and offer = ₹120, premium = ₹20 (20% of original price).\n- **Synergy allocation (example):** Given synergy = ₹30 and premium = ₹20 → Acquirer retains ₹10 (`30 − 20`); Target receives ₹20.\n\n### MCQ Trap Radar\n1. **Trap:** Target shareholders lose value because the acquirer pays a premium. → **Reality:** Target shareholders gain exactly the premium amount per share upon deal completion.\n2. **Trap:** Acquirer shareholders always lose value in M&A deals. → **Reality:** On average, acquiring firm shareholders break even; value creation occurs at the combined firm level.\n3. **Trap:** Target stock price rises to equal the offer price immediately upon announcement. → **Reality:** Target price typically settles below the offer price due to deal completion uncertainty.",
      "mcqs_json": "[]",
      "subjectives_json": "[]",
      "flashcards_json": "[]",
      "slides_json": "[]",
