      "video_id": "PYsa1p3vWqA",
      "duration_seconds": 243.49200000000002,
      "status": "completed",
      "notes_markdown": "# Help Tooltip in Charts\n\n> **Core Takeaway:** Help tooltips use a visible question mark to deliver longer instructions, such as color meanings, drill-down guidance, and data refresh timestamps, without cluttering the visual.\n### Help Tooltip Configuration\n- **Subtitle:** Always visible; best for short notes (e.g., \"red bars mean losses\").\n- **Help Tooltip:** Small question mark users click for extended instructions; ideal for drill-down guidance, data refresh dates, or issue alerts.\n- **Format Pane Path:** Select chart → Format pane → General → Header icons → enable **Help Tooltip** → enter custom text.\n- **Icon Control:** Users can toggle other header icons (drill up/down) on/off; help tooltip can remain active alongside them.\n\n### MCQ Trap Radar\n1. **Trap:** The help tooltip only shows static text and cannot include dynamic data like last refresh date.  \n   **Reality:** The tooltip field supports entering any text, including timestamps and data issue alerts.\n2. **Trap:** Enabling the help tooltip removes all other header icons from the chart.  \n   **Reality:** The help tooltip operates independently; other icons (drill up/down) remain visible unless manually turned off.",
      "mcqs_json": "[{\"id\": 1, \"question\": \"A business student is designing a Power BI report for new users who are unfamiliar with drill-down functionality. The student wants to include a brief note stating \\\"Red bars represent losses\\\" that is visible immediately without any user interaction. Which feature should the student use?\", \"options\": [\"A) Help Tooltip\", \"B) Subtitle\", \"C) Data Label\", \"D] Text Box\"], \"correct_index\": 1, \"difficulty\": \"Moderate | Tricky\", \"explanation\": \"The subtitle feature displays text permanently on the visual, making it ideal for short, always-visible notes like color meanings. The help tooltip requires user interaction (clicking the question mark) to become visible, so it is unsuitable for notes that must be seen immediately. The data label displays values associated with data points, and the text box, while possible, is not the standard feature for this purpose as per the lecture.\", \"key_concept\": \"Subtitle vs. Help Tooltip visibility\"}, {\"id\": 2, \"question\": \"When constructing a help tooltip in Power BI, which of the following can be effectively included to assist new users?\", \"options\": [\"A) Instructions on how to drill down into specific bars\", \"B) The exact formula used to calculate the metric displayed\", \"C) The name of the data source used for the visual\", \"D) A request for the user to contact IT support\"], \"correct_index\": 0, \"difficulty\": \"Easy | Conceptual\", \"explanation\": \"The lecture explicitly states that the help tooltip is suitable for longer instructions that would clutter the chart if placed in a subtitle, including educating users about functionalities like drilling down. The exact formula is not discussed in the context of tooltips, the data source name is a technical detail not meant for end-user instructions, and requesting IT support is not a standard or helpful tooltip content as per the professor's guidance.\", \"key_concept\": \"Help Tooltip content scope\"}, {\"id\": 3, \"question\": \"In the Power BI Format pane under General, a user toggles the help tooltip option to On. The user also wishes to hide the standard drill-down icon from the visual display. Which statement accurately describes the result?\", \"options\": [\"A) The help tooltip is disabled because the drill-down icon is hidden.\", \"B) The help tooltip remains active and independent of the drill-down icon visibility setting.\", \"C) The subtitle automatically replaces the help tooltip.\", \"D) The chart becomes unresponsive to user clicks.\"], \"correct_index\": 1, \"difficulty\": \"Moderate | Tricky\", \"explanation\": \"The lecture demonstrates that the help tooltip setting is found in the Format pane and can be turned on independently of other icons. The professor states that other icons (like drill up/down) can be turned off while the help tooltip remains active, allowing the instructor to show only the question mark method of interaction. The settings are not mutually exclusive.\", \"key_concept\": \"Independent configuration of chart icons and tooltips\"}, {\"id\": 4, \"question\": \"A professor adds the text \\\"Red bars show losses. Use the tooltip to drill down into specific bars\\\" to the help tooltip of a chart. Later, the data is refreshed and the red bars now represent profits due to a change in business strategy. Which action should the professor take to keep the report accurate?\", \"options\": [\"A) Nothing, the help tooltip text is permanent and never needs updating.\", \"B) Update the help tooltip text to reflect the new meaning of the red bars.\", \"C) Delete the help tooltip and rely solely on the subtitle.\", \"D) Change the color of the bars to green instead.\"], \"correct_index\": 1, \"difficulty\": \"Easy | Conceptual\", \"explanation\": \"The lecture emphasizes that the help tooltip is a useful location for noting data issues or instructions to users. If the underlying data meaning changes (e.g., red bars no longer mean losses), the instructional text in the help tooltip becomes misleading and must be updated to maintain report accuracy and user guidance. Leaving incorrect instructions violates the principle of data transparency.\", \"key_concept\": \"Help Tooltip as a data transparency tool\"}]",
      "subjectives_json": "[]",
      "flashcards_json": "[]",
      "slides_json": "[]",
