          "front": "Why is IRR called the \"internal\" rate of return?",
          "back": "IRR is called internal because its calculation requires only the magnitude and timing of cash flows internal to the project. It does not require the opportunity cost of capital for the calculation itself, though the decision rule requires comparing IRR to the opportunity cost of capital."
