          "explanation": "The correct answer is C. The OLI framework predicts that when a firm is strong only on ownership advantages (O), it is better off exporting. If the firm had ownership (O) plus location advantages (L), it could consider licensing. FDI is only predicted when the firm has advantages on all three dimensions: ownership (O), location (L), and internalisation (I). Therefore, with only O advantages, exporting is the predicted mode.",
          "key_concept": "OLI Framework: O alone → Exporting"
