          "explanation": "The correct answer is B) This question tests the conceptual distinction between user-interface filtering and author-level filtering. Slicers are visual components placed on the report page that end-users interact with directly to segment data. The Filters pane, by contrast, is used during report authoring to set default filters that typically run in the background; viewers generally cannot right-click or toggle these filters off during presentation. Option A is incorrect because slicers are not used for data preparation (that is done in Power Query). Option C is a distractor as aesthetic appeal is not the primary functional difference. Option D is incorrect because the functional scope differs significantly (page-level vs. report-level).",
          "key_concept": "User-driven (Slicer) vs. Author-driven (Filters Pane) filtering"
