          "explanation": "The correct answer is B) The slicer filters the underlying dataset to include only records where the Year field equals 2021. The line chart, being connected to the same dataset, automatically recalculates and displays only the monthly sales values that correspond to 2021. Option A is incorrect as data is present; it is just filtered. Option C is a distractor; the chart type (line) remains a line chart, showing the temporal pattern for the selected year, not a single aggregated total. Option D is incorrect because the whole point of a slicer is to change the displayed data.",
          "key_concept": "Slicer-driven dataset filtering and visual update"
